ey (Malek), who is tasked with determining whether Nazi prisoners are fit to stand trial for their war crimes and finds himself in a complex battle of wits with Hermann Goring (Crowe), Hitler's right-hand man.\",\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalized\",\"sdTrailers\":[{\"url\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/mp4/364682_uk_high.mp4\",\"__typename\":\"MovieVideo\"}],\"hdTrailers\":[{\"url\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/QuickTime/364682_uk_hd.mov\",\"__typename\":\"MovieVideo\"}],\"poster\":{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/5f/8f/5f8fe2a51769813b7aede018498d01e0.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},\"cmsAssets\":{\"__typename\":\"CMSAsset\",\"images\":[{\"type\":\"DEFAULT_HERO_IMAGE\",\"url\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/2/2f108b699c243e689b2bda99ff394558.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"BOAppImage\"}]}},\"exhibitor\":{\"title\":null,\"poster\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/ffe2e34bb301110a374d21a520c1aa37.jpg\",\"synopsis\":\"Nuremberg chronicles the true story of the eponymous trials held by the Allies against the defeated Nazi regime. The film centres on American psychiatrist Douglas Kelley (Malek), who is tasked with determining whether Nazi prisoners are fit to stand trial for their war crimes and finds himself in a complex battle of wits with Hermann Goring (Crowe), Hitler's right-hand man.\",\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalizedOverride\",\"images\":[]},\"originalTitle\":\"Nuremberg\",\"synopsis\":\"Nuremberg chronicles the true story of the eponymous trials held by the Allies against the defeated Nazi regime. The film centres on American psychiatrist Douglas Kelley (Malek), who is tasked with determining whether Nazi prisoners are fit to stand trial for their war crimes and finds himself in a complex battle of wits with Hermann Goring (Crowe), Hitler's right-hand man.\",\"certificate\":\"15\",\"casting\":[\"Rami Malek\",\"Russell Crowe\",\"Michael Shannon\",\"Richard E. Grant\",\"Leo Woodall\",\"John Slattery\",\"Lydia Peckham\",\"Wrenn Schmidt\",\"Lotte Verbeek\",\"Andreas Pietschmann\"],\"direction\":[\"James Vanderbilt\"],\"coDirection\":[],\"pictures\":[\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/a7/53/a75364399b52a50b0bd2b84da968dd01.PNG\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/10/63/10638b87c447d320fbb7988dd725d324.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/96/b7/96b7f0cac1305ef3a4889a83e6b84e36.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/97/fc/97fc5824fd8801bc122cf7ce92f9c8f6.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/a4/b4/a4b4a9714d340cc38f117ef4d99491f9.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/23/ca/23ca0df78ea401a00726bcb4f650f605.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/bd/49/bd495926d0dcd2505728e34113a1937b.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/43/3e/433e9c2e9080fb0bba14c2abc4a9e739.jpg\"],\"heroImages\":[\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/2/2f108b699c243e689b2bda99ff394558.jpg\"],\"release\":\"2025-11-14T00:00:00.000Z\",\"advisory\":\"images of real dead bodies, Holocaust references, strong violence\",\"trailer\":{\"SD\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/mp4/364682_uk_high.mp4\",\"HD\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/QuickTime/364682_uk_hd.mov\"},\"localizations\":[],\"studio\":{\"name\":\"Sky Pictures\"}},{\"id\":\"311364\",\"title\":\"One Battle After Another\",\"runtime\":9720,\"genres\":\"Action\",\"__typename\":\"Movie\",\"altId\":[\"372340\",\"388380\"],\"coDirectors\":{\"nodes\":[],\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\"},\"quadImages\":[],\"poster\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/06708b1f461d7eea4d8b47a2a6acadb7.jpg\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/ac/0e/ac0e9fb6be8de62fd6a6dae074acf96c.JPG\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/29/5b/295ba89bab8d647a67198b3b19fd4714.JPG\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/5f/65/5f65b25b7afc3e157f406c3c72190f04.JPG\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/6f/7d/6f7d90af046a63aab2bfba46e472e59d.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/f9/fb/f9fbb3ec5e84edb81cb9d875d940187b.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/0b/c7/0bc7edaf104d11e13019118ff1afaf50.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/07/45/07458fd5e1816838fe87956514c2d531.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"}],\"directors\":{\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\",\"nodes\":[{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"person\":{\"firstName\":\"Paul Thomas\",\"lastName\":\"Anderson\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"}}]},\"cast\":{\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\",\"nodes\":[{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Leonardo\",\"lastName\":\"DiCaprio\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Benicio\",\"lastName\":\"Del Toro\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Teyana\",\"lastName\":\"Taylor\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Sean\",\"lastName\":\"Penn\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Regina\",\"lastName\":\"Hall\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Chase\",\"lastName\":\"Infiniti\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Alana\",\"lastName\":\"Haim\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"D.W.\",\"lastName\":\"Moffett\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Paul\",\"lastName\":\"Grimstad\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"James\",\"lastName\":\"Raterman\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null}]},\"releases\":[{\"releasedAt\":\"2025-09-26T00:00:00.000Z\",\"__typename\":\"Release\",\"distributors\":[{\"id\":\"13759\",\"name\":\"Warner Bros U.K.\",\"__typename\":\"Company\"}],\"rating\":{\"advisory\":\"strong language, sex references, violence, references to sexual violence\",\"__typename\":\"Rating\",\"certificate\":\"15\"},\"localRatings\":[]}],\"embargoes\":[],\"locale\":{\"title\":\"One Battle After Another\",\"synopsis\":\"Washed-up revolutionary Bob (DiCaprio) exists in a state of stoned paranoia, surviving off-grid with his spirited, self-reliant daughter, Willa (Infiniti).  When his evil nemesis (Penn) resurfaces after 16 years and she goes missing, the former radical scrambles to find her, father and daughter both battling the consequences of his past.\",\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalized\",\"sdTrailers\":[{\"url\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/mp4/372340_uk_high.mp4\",\"__typename\":\"MovieVideo\"}],\"hdTrailers\":[{\"url\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/QuickTime/372340_uk_hd.mov\",\"__typename\":\"MovieVideo\"}],\"poster\":{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/4e/a0/4ea09925e3ecebbf056642378f14ee8f.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},\"cmsAssets\":{\"__typename\":\"CMSAsset\",\"images\":[{\"type\":\"DEFAULT_HERO_IMAGE\",\"url\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/2/d73264679f9d595629f98d5b45147563.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"BOAppImage\"}]}},\"exhibitor\":{\"title\":null,\"poster\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/06708b1f461d7eea4d8b47a2a6acadb7.jpg\",\"synopsis\":\"Directed, written, & produced by Paul Thomas Anderson, One Battle After Another is a sprawling action-thriller about revolution, redemption, and the ghosts of past battles. With an all star cast including Leonardo DiCaprio, Sean Penn, Regina Hall, Teyana Taylor, Benicio del Toro, and many more.\\n\\nBob Ferguson (Leonardo DiCaprio) is a washed-up revolutionary who lives in a state of stoned paranoia, following a violent fall-out with his nemesis,  and has been surviving off-grid for 16 years with his spirited and self-reliant daughter, Willa (Chase Infiniti).\\n\\nWhen his old nemesis Colonel Steven J. Lockjaw (Sean Penn) resurfaces, and Willa suddenly goes missing, Bob (DiCaprio) is forced to assemble his old comrades and battle the consequences of their pasts that he has long tried to outrun, in order to rescue his daughter.\",\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalizedOverride\",\"images\":[{\"type\":\"DEFAULT_STILL\",\"url\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/852d283a4f2dbb3e8dc2ff2a34f57475.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"BOAppImage\"}]},\"originalTitle\":\"One Battle After Another\",\"synopsis\":\"Directed, written, & produced by Paul Thomas Anderson, One Battle After Another is a sprawling action-thriller about revolution, redemption, and the ghosts of past battles. With an all star cast including Leonardo DiCaprio, Sean Penn, Regina Hall, Teyana Taylor, Benicio del Toro, and many more.\\n\\nBob Ferguson (Leonardo DiCaprio) is a washed-up revolutionary who lives in a state of stoned paranoia, following a violent fall-out with his nemesis,  and has been surviving off-grid for 16 years with his spirited and self-reliant daughter, Willa (Chase Infiniti).\\n\\nWhen his old nemesis Colonel Steven J. Lockjaw (Sean Penn) resurfaces, and Willa suddenly goes missing, Bob (DiCaprio) is forced to assemble his old comrades and battle the consequences of their pasts that he has long tried to outrun, in order to rescue his daughter.\",\"certificate\":\"15\",\"casting\":[\"Leonardo DiCaprio\",\"Benicio Del Toro\",\"Teyana Taylor\",\"Sean Penn\",\"Regina Hall\",\"Chase Infiniti\",\"Alana Haim\",\"D.W. Moffett\",\"Paul Grimstad\",\"James Raterman\"],\"direction\":[\"Paul Thomas Anderson\"],\"coDirection\":[],\"pictures\":[\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/852d283a4f2dbb3e8dc2ff2a34f57475.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/ac/0e/ac0e9fb6be8de62fd6a6dae074acf96c.JPG\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/29/5b/295ba89bab8d647a67198b3b19fd4714.JPG\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/5f/65/5f65b25b7afc3e157f406c3c72190f04.JPG\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/6f/7d/6f7d90af046a63aab2bfba46e472e59d.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/f9/fb/f9fbb3ec5e84edb81cb9d875d940187b.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/0b/c7/0bc7edaf104d11e13019118ff1afaf50.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/07/45/07458fd5e1816838fe87956514c2d531.jpg\"],\"heroImages\":[\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/852d283a4f2dbb3e8dc2ff2a34f57475.jpg\",\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/2/d73264679f9d595629f98d5b45147563.jpg\"],\"release\":\"2025-09-26T00:00:00.000Z\",\"advisory\":\"strong language, sex references, violence, references to sexual violence\",\"trailer\":{\"SD\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/mp4/372340_uk_high.mp4\",\"HD\":\"https://m.boxoffice.media/QuickTime/372340_uk_hd.mov\"},\"localizations\":[],\"studio\":{\"name\":\"Warner Bros U.K.\"}},{\"id\":\"2072\",\"title\":\"One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest\",\"runtime\":7740,\"genres\":\"Drama\",\"poster\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/5808c35db39ce35e7d2073085f0d38ff.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Movie\",\"altId\":[\"6111\"],\"coDirectors\":{\"nodes\":[],\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\"},\"quadImages\":[],\"images\":[{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/pictures/14/02/26/13/47/055754.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889063.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889062.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889061.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889060.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889059.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889058.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889057.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889056.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889055.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"}],\"directors\":{\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\",\"nodes\":[{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"person\":{\"firstName\":\"Milos\",\"lastName\":\"Forman\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"}}]},\"cast\":{\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\",\"nodes\":[{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Jack\",\"lastName\":\"Nicholson\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Louise\",\"lastName\":\"Fletcher\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"William\",\"lastName\":\"Redfield\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Brad\",\"lastName\":\"Dourif\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Will\",\"lastName\":\"Sampson\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Christopher\",\"lastName\":\"Lloyd\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Danny\",\"lastName\":\"DeVito\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Dean R.\",\"lastName\":\"Brooks\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Peter\",\"lastName\":\"Brocco\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Michael\",\"lastName\":\"Berryman\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null}]},\"releases\":[{\"releasedAt\":\"2017-04-14T00:00:00.000Z\",\"__typename\":\"Release\",\"distributors\":[{\"id\":\"9597\",\"name\":\"BFI Distribution\",\"__typename\":\"Company\"}],\"rating\":{\"advisory\":\"very strong language, strong violence\",\"__typename\":\"Rating\",\"certificate\":\"15\"},\"localRatings\":[]}],\"embargoes\":[],\"locale\":{\"title\":\"One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest\",\"synopsis\":\"\",\"poster\":null,\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalized\",\"sdTrailers\":[],\"hdTrailers\":[],\"cmsAssets\":{\"__typename\":\"CMSAsset\",\"images\":[]}},\"exhibitor\":{\"title\":null,\"poster\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/5808c35db39ce35e7d2073085f0d38ff.jpg\",\"synopsis\":\"Selected by the Casting Directors Branch, Everyman presents: One Flew Over The Cuckoo's Nest.\\n\\nWhen free-spirited petty crook Randle P. McMurphy (Jack Nicholson) arrives at the state mental hospital, his contagious sense of disorder jolts the routine. He's on one side of a brewing war, soft-spoken, coolly monstrous Nurse Ratched (Louis Fletcher) on the other. At stake is the fate of every patient in the ward.\\n\\nJack Nicholson won his first Oscar for his vibrant portrayal of the rebellious R. P. McMurphy in director Milos Forman’s Best Picture-winning film version of Ken Kesey’s popular novel set in a mental institution. Casting directors Mike Fenton and Jane Feinberg helped fill the screen with an impressively vivid ensemble, including Best Actress winner Louise Fletcher, Supporting Actor nominee Brad Dourif, Christopher Lloyd, Danny DeVito, Scatman Crothers, and Will Sampson. \\n\\nRestored in 2025 by the Academy Film Archive, with restoration funding provided by Teatro Della Pace Film and special thanks to Paul Zaentz, the feature returns to the big screen in 4k at Everyman The Whiteley on Thursday, 9 October.\",\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalizedOverride\",\"images\":[{\"type\":\"DEFAULT_STILL\",\"url\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/1e66a7a39c5d3850a388942f873385c4.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"BOAppImage\"}]},\"originalTitle\":\"One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest\",\"synopsis\":\"Selected by the Casting Directors Branch, Everyman presents: One Flew Over The Cuckoo's Nest.\\n\\nWhen free-spirited petty crook Randle P. McMurphy (Jack Nicholson) arrives at the state mental hospital, his contagious sense of disorder jolts the routine. He's on one side of a brewing war, soft-spoken, coolly monstrous Nurse Ratched (Louis Fletcher) on the other. At stake is the fate of every patient in the ward.\\n\\nJack Nicholson won his first Oscar for his vibrant portrayal of the rebellious R. P. McMurphy in director Milos Forman’s Best Picture-winning film version of Ken Kesey’s popular novel set in a mental institution. Casting directors Mike Fenton and Jane Feinberg helped fill the screen with an impressively vivid ensemble, including Best Actress winner Louise Fletcher, Supporting Actor nominee Brad Dourif, Christopher Lloyd, Danny DeVito, Scatman Crothers, and Will Sampson. \\n\\nRestored in 2025 by the Academy Film Archive, with restoration funding provided by Teatro Della Pace Film and special thanks to Paul Zaentz, the feature returns to the big screen in 4k at Everyman The Whiteley on Thursday, 9 October.\",\"certificate\":\"15\",\"casting\":[\"Jack Nicholson\",\"Louise Fletcher\",\"William Redfield\",\"Brad Dourif\",\"Will Sampson\",\"Christopher Lloyd\",\"Danny DeVito\",\"Dean R. Brooks\",\"Peter Brocco\",\"Michael Berryman\"],\"direction\":[\"Milos Forman\"],\"coDirection\":[],\"pictures\":[\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/1e66a7a39c5d3850a388942f873385c4.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/pictures/14/02/26/13/47/055754.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889063.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889062.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889061.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889060.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889059.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889058.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889057.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889056.jpg\",\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/medias/nmedia/18/87/08/25/19889055.jpg\"],\"heroImages\":[\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/1e66a7a39c5d3850a388942f873385c4.jpg\"],\"release\":\"2017-04-14T00:00:00.000Z\",\"advisory\":\"very strong language, strong violence\",\"trailer\":{\"SD\":null,\"HD\":null},\"localizations\":[],\"studio\":{\"name\":\"BFI Distribution\"}},{\"id\":\"1000032192\",\"title\":\"PARIS 75 - The European Cup Final Football Tried To Forget\",\"runtime\":5880,\"genres\":\"Documentary\",\"poster\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/4a6eb9dd8ed1a543ba84e4655e6f4ca5.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Movie\",\"altId\":[\"402016\"],\"coDirectors\":{\"nodes\":[],\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\"},\"images\":[],\"quadImages\":[],\"directors\":{\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\",\"nodes\":[{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"person\":{\"firstName\":\"Harvey\",\"lastName\":\"Marcus\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"}}]},\"cast\":{\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\",\"nodes\":[{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Mark\",\"lastName\":\"Leech\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Paul\",\"lastName\":\"Reaney\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Allan\",\"lastName\":\"Clarke\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null},{\"__typename\":\"MovieCredit\",\"actor\":{\"firstName\":\"Margaret\",\"lastName\":\"Clark\",\"__typename\":\"Person\"},\"originalVoiceActor\":null,\"localizedVoiceActor\":null}]},\"releases\":[{\"releasedAt\":\"2025-10-09T00:00:00.000Z\",\"distributors\":[],\"__typename\":\"Release\",\"rating\":{\"advisory\":null,\"__typename\":\"Rating\",\"certificate\":\"12A\"},\"localRatings\":[]}],\"embargoes\":[],\"locale\":{\"title\":\"Paris 75- Gala Screening\",\"synopsis\":\"Join us for the Gala Screening of PARIS 75 - The European Cup Final Football Tried To Forget on Thursday 9th October from 7pm.\\n \\nThe pre-film ‘warm-up’ starts with a live-set from Leeds United’s very-own Punjabi singing-sensation Jinder Jade, and the rare opportunity to be photographed with the original shirt worn by Peter Lorimer in the 1975 final, before joining stars of the documentary for the PARIS 75 world premiere.\",\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalized\",\"sdTrailers\":[],\"hdTrailers\":[],\"poster\":{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/3d/8b/3d8bdb90d2ba32cfdf84f9041724fb20.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},\"cmsAssets\":{\"__typename\":\"CMSAsset\",\"images\":[]}},\"exhibitor\":{\"title\":\"PARIS 75 - The European Cup Final Football Tried To Forget\",\"poster\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/4a6eb9dd8ed1a543ba84e4655e6f4ca5.jpg\",\"synopsis\":\"‘Moving. Powerful. Magnificent!’ – Adam Pope, BBC Sport\\n‘Enlightening and compelling.’ – Graham Smyth, Yorkshire Evening Post\\n\\nFifty years on, at each and every game, Leeds United fans still sing the same refrain, ‘We Are The Champions, Champions Of Europe’.\\n\\nPARIS 75 – The European Cup Final Football Tried To Forget, takes a unique look at a season and, ultimately, a match steeped in controversy and myth which defined the identity of a club, its supporters and, arguably, a city, that endures to this day; bringing to a crashing end an era in football never witnessed before or since.\\n\\nAs much about the history and heritage of football from a bygone age, PARIS 75 features rare and never-seen-before cine-footage taken by supporters who followed Leeds across Europe that season and exclusive home-video from Leeds United legend Paul Reaney; it is the story of female football supporting pioneers and early foreign travel, a film about football in the Seventies, with appeal to Leeds United fans and neutrals alike. It is a film for the fans told by the fans who were there – Roy, Carole, Rich, Margaret and Heidi; Leeds United and England legends, Paul Reaney and Allan Clarke, who played, and other key figures who witnessed that season and that final.\\n\\nAt a time when supporters have never felt so alienated and distanced from today’s supercar-driving, noise-cancelling players of today and the anonymous corporates who own their club, PARIS 75 is a timely reminder of what football used to be – the good and the bad.\",\"__typename\":\"MovieLocalizedOverride\",\"images\":[]},\"originalTitle\":\"Paris 75- Gala Screening\",\"synopsis\":\"‘Moving. Powerful. Magnificent!’ – Adam Pope, BBC Sport\\n‘Enlightening and compelling.’ – Graham Smyth, Yorkshire Evening Post\\n\\nFifty years on, at each and every game, Leeds United fans still sing the same refrain, ‘We Are The Champions, Champions Of Europe’.\\n\\nPARIS 75 – The European Cup Final Football Tried To Forget, takes a unique look at a season and, ultimately, a match steeped in controversy and myth which defined the identity of a club, its supporters and, arguably, a city, that endures to this day; bringing to a crashing end an era in football never witnessed before or since.\\n\\nAs much about the history and heritage of football from a bygone age, PARIS 75 features rare and never-seen-before cine-footage taken by supporters who followed Leeds across Europe that season and exclusive home-video from Leeds United legend Paul Reaney; it is the story of female football supporting pioneers and early foreign travel, a film about football in the Seventies, with appeal to Leeds United fans and neutrals alike. It is a film for the fans told by the fans who were there – Roy, Carole, Rich, Margaret and Heidi; Leeds United and England legends, Paul Reaney and Allan Clarke, who played, and other key figures who witnessed that season and that final.\\n\\nAt a time when supporters have never felt so alienated and distanced from today’s supercar-driving, noise-cancelling players of today and the anonymous corporates who own their club, PARIS 75 is a timely reminder of what football used to be – the good and the bad.\",\"certificate\":\"12A\",\"casting\":[\"Mark Leech\",\"Paul Reaney\",\"Allan Clarke\",\"Margaret Clark\"],\"direction\":[\"Harvey Marcus\"],\"coDirection\":[],\"pictures\":[],\"heroImages\":[],\"release\":\"2025-10-09T00:00:00.000Z\",\"advisory\":null,\"trailer\":{\"SD\":null,\"HD\":null},\"localizations\":[],\"studio\":{}},{\"id\":\"1000004723\",\"title\":\"Pets on a Train\",\"runtime\":5160,\"genres\":\"Animation, Family\",\"__typename\":\"Movie\",\"altId\":[\"366031\"],\"coDirectors\":{\"nodes\":[],\"__typename\":\"CreditsPager\"},\"poster\":\"https://cms-assets.webediamovies.pro/production/279/ac6a8498beb46430b5b25d26c3ec47a9.jpg\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"https://all.web.img.acsta.net/img/b8/09/b809bf1aac34c4a4fd89a84ec1c922ab.jpg\",\"__typename\":\"Image\"},{\"url\":\"https://a